{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.OrthoschemeTiling","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetFacesFromInscribedTriangle","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetEqChimney"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume.region_eq_chimney_is_restrictive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume.region_eq_chimney_is_restrictive","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MostowIdealTetVolume.lean#L214-L236","doc":"**The dihedral-angle field is genuinely restrictive (§3b-tax non-degeneracy).**\nThe whole space `ℝ³` cannot be a `region_eq_chimney` region: a chimney lies inside\nthe upper half-space (`chimney_subset_upperHalfSpace`), so the point at height `-1`\nis in `univ` but in no chimney.  Together with `tetDihedralAngles` requiring the\n*correct* vertex angles, the class asserts real content — it is not\nauto-satisfiable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume.idealTetVolume_fires","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume.idealTetVolume_fires","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MostowIdealTetVolume.lean#L200-L212","doc":"**`idealTetVolume_eq_lambda_sum` fires unconditionally** — confirming the\nclass is inhabited by the real instance above.  For the Milnor-normalized\nideal-tetrahedron region of acute dihedral angles `(α, β, γ)`, the genuine\nhyperbolic volume is `Λ(α) + Λ(β) + Λ(γ)`.\n\nClosed modulo the cited totally-geodesic / normalized-position identification (the\none fact Mathlib cannot express); everything else is Lean-proved, sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume.idealTetVolume_of_vertices","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume.idealTetVolume_of_vertices","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MostowIdealTetVolume.lean#L171-L198","doc":"**T2, UNCONDITIONAL (no class) — the volume of the independently-defined ideal\ntetrahedron.**  For an acute admissible triple `α + β + γ = π`, the genuine hyperbolic\nvolume `dx dy dz / z³` of the vertex-defined region\n`idealTetrahedron (circlePoint 1 t) (circlePoint 1 (t+2γ)) (circlePoint 1 (t+2γ+2α))`\nis `Λ(α) + Λ(β) + Λ(γ)`.\n\nThis does **not** go through the `MostowIdealTetVolume` class: the region is defined\nfrom its four ideal vertices (File A2), proved equal to the chimney (File A3), and the\nchimney's volume is the already-proved `hypVolume_chimney_inscribedTriangle`.  The\nclass above is now *optional* — a labelled §3b-cond packaging — since the volume\nidentity holds unconditionally for the concrete region.  Closed modulo the single\ncited totally-geodesic model-faithfulness fact (File A1); everything else is\nLean-proved, sorry-free.\n\nThe acuteness here is REAL, unlike the acuteness `idealTet_eq_chimney` used to\ncarry: it is consumed by `hypVolume_chimney_inscribedTriangle`, whose wedges need\n`ψ < π/2`.  The obtuse companion is\n`ObtuseTiling.idealTetVolume_of_vertices_obtuse`, which swaps that one step for\nthe obtuse tiling and is otherwise the same two lines. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume.instMostowIdealTetVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume.instMostowIdealTetVolume","kind":"instance","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MostowIdealTetVolume.lean#L142-L169","doc":"**The REAL instance — now with the region-equality PROVED, not adopted.**  The\nideal-tetrahedron region is the *independently defined* `idealTetrahedron` of File A2\n(the intersection of four geodesic half-spaces built from the four ideal vertices),\nNOT a chimney by fiat.  `region_eq_chimney` is now discharged by the **proved**\nset-equality `idealTet_eq_chimney` (File A3) — a genuine theorem replacing the former\n`rfl` — and `tetDihedralAngles` by the File-4 proof that the chimney's three ∞-edge\ndihedral angles are `(α, β, γ)`.\n\nThis is the anti-laundering content twice over: the region is an independent object,\nand BOTH class fields are proved (the region-equality is no longer definitional).  It\ncloses T2 **modulo the single cited totally-geodesic / normalized-position\nidentification** (relocated to File A1's `geodesicPlaneThrough` — a definition with a\ncitation, not an axiom or `sorry`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume.idealTetVolume_eq_lambda_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume.idealTetVolume_eq_lambda_sum","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MostowIdealTetVolume.lean#L123-L140","doc":"**T2, on the class (§3b-cond).**  The genuine hyperbolic volume\n`dx dy dz / z³` of the ideal-tetrahedron region of acute dihedral angles\n`(α, β, γ)` equals `Λ(α) + Λ(β) + Λ(γ)`.\n\n**Derived, not assumed**: the class supplies only that the region is a chimney\n(`region_eq_chimney`); the volume value comes from the already-PROVED, sorry-free\n`hypVolume_chimney_inscribedTriangle`.  The proof does real work — `rw` the region\nidentity, then discharge with the proved analytic theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume.MostowIdealTetVolume.tetDihedralAngles","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume.MostowIdealTetVolume.tetDihedralAngles","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MostowIdealTetVolume.lean#L113-L113","doc":"**The dihedral-angle content (PROVED in File 4 for the realizing chimney).**\nThere is a normalized position `t` in which the region is the chimney over the\ninscribed triangle AND the three ∞-edge dihedral angles — the hyperbolic angles\nbetween the interior edge-perpendicular in-face vectors of the pairs of vertical\nfaces — are exactly `(α, β, γ)`.  This is the real geometric content the class\nrequires of an instance; it is discharged by\n`chimney_infedge_dihedral_eq_vertexAngle`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume.MostowIdealTetVolume.region_eq_chimney","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume.MostowIdealTetVolume.region_eq_chimney","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MostowIdealTetVolume.lean#L103-L103","doc":"**Milnor's normalization (cited geometric input).**  For an acute admissible\ntriple, the region equals the vertical chimney over the inscribed triangle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume.MostowIdealTetVolume.tetRegion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume.MostowIdealTetVolume.tetRegion","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MostowIdealTetVolume.lean#L100-L100","doc":"The region an ideal tetrahedron of dihedral angles `(α, β, γ)` occupies in\nthe upper half-space `H³`, in Milnor's normalized position. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume.MostowIdealTetVolume.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume.MostowIdealTetVolume.mk","kind":"ctor","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MostowIdealTetVolume.lean#L97-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume.MostowIdealTetVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MostowIdealTetVolume.MostowIdealTetVolume","kind":"class","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MostowIdealTetVolume.lean#L83-L121","doc":"**The ideal-tetrahedron region + its dihedral angles, as a §3b conditional\nclass.**\n\nA datum supplies, for every acute admissible dihedral-angle triple `(α, β, γ)`,\nthe region `tetRegion α β γ` that a genuine ideal tetrahedron of those dihedral\nangles occupies in Milnor's normalized position, together with:\n\n* `region_eq_chimney`: the region IS a vertical chimney over the inscribed\n  triangle (Milnor's normalization — the cited geometric input); and\n* `tetDihedralAngles`: the region's **three ∞-edge dihedral angles are\n  `(α, β, γ)`** — the real geometric content, PROVED in File 4 for the chimney\n  (`chimney_infedge_dihedral_eq_vertexAngle`).  This field carries the dihedral\n  angles, not the volume conclusion, and cannot be met by an arbitrary chimney\n  over the wrong triangle. ","signatureChunk":0}]}